     "compare",
     "savings"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Shireen has ₹150 and adds ₹100 each week. After four weeks she adds 4 × 100 = 400.\n150 + 400 = 550. She has ₹550.\nPeter uncle saved ₹250, ₹125 and ₹350 in three months. Add them: 250 + 125 = 375, then 375 + 350 = 725. He saved ₹725.\nEstimate answers to the nearest hundred first. 156 + 34 is about 200, and 500 - 395 is about 100.\nCompare expressions without calculating. 373 + 40 is more than 373 + 23 because 40 is bigger.\nNumber cards 0 to 5 can make two 3-digit numbers. Add or subtract and try to get the biggest sum or smallest difference."
    }
   },
